{"c":[{"id":"bae047d115123a98","sum":"D2-02/B27: no routing = producers self-trigger; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle, routedSettled). Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip run to run; diff per moment. Failed fills reach the user only via Helper.fillFailed.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"3ae20362fc05a5eb","sum":"D2-02/B27: routing absent keeps producers self-triggering; routed producers hold offers until chosen (await routing.idle then routedSettled). B17/B18 memory held-out sets label own First/Last 'none'; score with relabelled copies in evidence/screen/b27/memsets.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261004T233521Z-ca79b84757c7cc74","text":"D2-02: HelperOptions.routing absent keeps producers self-triggering (tests, producer evals); main.ts routes when Jev is on. Routed producers hold offers (engine.release/dropHeld, openApp.showHeld, events.judge); await routing.idle() then routedSettled.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261004T235441Z-17480ff5b594d902","text":"B27: B17/B18 memory held-out sets label the user's own First/Last name fields 'none' (written when fill copied values only whole); score them with the relabelled copies in ~/.caret-run/evidence/screen/b27/memsets, whose about-fill-eval accepts expect first/last.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"ccba801a8aa9c8ea","sum":"D2-02/B27: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of the 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs; diff runs per moment before crediting a code change. A failed fill reaches the user only via Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); ids go to warn.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T031924Z-459c6ef9ec89ae5d","text":"D2-02: Router 1 answers within ~0.05 of its 0.5 floor flip between live corpus runs (m02 0.52/0.49, m09 0.45/0.51); diff runs per moment before crediting a code change with a recall move.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T032639Z-5905894b0fafbfcc","text":"B27: a failed fill reaches the user only through Helper.fillFailed (planner/says.ts fillSays); its window and field ids go to warn. Early exits that called this.error published ids until afadd34.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"9e36f49db21c9173","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates, site.waitForLoad the landed page before the next site.command (else it hits the old page's poll). Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: trust a scope only if the whole instruction is a grammar sentence.","tree":{"c":[{"id":"91fb33162eeab888","sum":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or it hits the departing page's long poll and times out. (B28's 'accept.ts cannot run executor.run' was lifted in D2-04.)","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044215Z-74ca06dede7d18b3","text":"B28: after a fixture page navigates away, wait for site.waitForLoad of the landed page before the next site.command, or the command goes to the departing page's long poll and times out.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T044215Z-8ef7ae66324e8796","text":"B28: accept.ts cannot run executor.run: it first asks the native reader for watchInput and gets noWindow; check page-link VerbResults in accept and the executor with test/fake-app.ts knobs.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"},{"id":"e2fcc93ff7d0331d","sum":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists. Whole-form or section scope is trusted only if the whole normalized instruction is a grammar sentence (only FILLER beside the phrase; sources open with a preposition). Label matching and strip-then-search failed open.","tree":{"c":[{"name":"20261005T044915Z-bf6a7f62ff27c59b","text":"B28: Ask scope words (planner/scope-words.ts) are allowlists: only FILLER may stand beside a whole-form or section phrase, and a source phrase must open with a preposition. Matching field labels in the rest failed open three times.","type":"note"},{"name":"20261005T060231Z-5982020e0a78f148","text":"B28: Ask trusts a whole-form or section scope only if the whole normalized instruction is a scope-words.ts grammar sentence, and a section only under one un-nested heading that is wholly the user's own. Searching inside after stripping sources/titles/quotes failed open 5 times.","type":"note"}]},"type":"nap"}]},"type":"nap"}]}
